From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: set CTL_TOP group id from DPU 5.0

The vendor driver for this SoC appears not to write bits 31:28 of CTL_TOP
(sde_hw_ctl.c starts from mode_sel = 0 and only ORs BIT(17) for cmd mode),
so this was initially assumed to be wrong and a candidate for removal.

Testing on the device proved otherwise: a build without this change is
clearly worse (the whole screen is corrupted during early boot), so the
group id does need to be programmed on DPU 6.9. Motorola presumably sets
it somewhere that was not found in the downstream tree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_ctl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_ctl.c
@@ -581,8 +581,13 @@
 	/* CTL_TOP[31:28] carries group_id to collate CTL paths
 	 * per VM. Explicitly disable it until VM support is
 	 * added in SW. Power on reset value is not disable.
+	 *
+	 * The register and the field have existed since DPU 5.0 (the targets
+	 * with CTL_CFG_VERSION_1_0_0), and the downstream driver writes 0xF on
+	 * all of them. Leaving it at 0 groups this CTL with group 0, so it can
+	 * end up waiting on other CTL paths and never complete the frame.
 	 */
-	if (ctx->mdss_ver->core_major_ver >= 7)
+	if (ctx->mdss_ver->core_major_ver >= 5)
 		mode_sel = CTL_DEFAULT_GROUP_ID  << 28;
 
 	if (cfg->intf_mode_sel == DPU_CTL_MODE_SEL_CMD)
